[Attached Table 1] <Amended July 26, 2017>

Schedule of Authorized Staff of the Commission (Related to Article 2(1))

<table>
<tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>120</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Political-service subtotal</strong></td><td>5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chairperson</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vice-chairperson</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Standing commissioners</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>General-service, special-service and specific-service subtotal</strong></td><td>115</td></tr>
<tr><td>Senior officials or special-service officials belonging to the Senior Executive Service</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deputy director general or secretary</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Secretary, prosecutorial investigation secretary, technical secretary, or special-service official equivalent to Grade IV</td><td>8</td></tr>
<tr><td>Administrative officer, deputy audit officer, prosecutorial officer, investigation officer, information systems officer, social welfare officer, public health officer, maritime and fisheries officer, police superintendent, or special-service official equivalent to Grade V</td><td>23</td></tr>
<tr><td>Administrative senior officer, audit senior officer, prosecutorial senior officer, broadcasting and telecommunications senior officer, information systems senior officer, records researcher, social welfare senior officer, public health senior officer, maritime and fisheries senior officer, police senior inspector, or special-service official equivalent to Grade VI</td><td>38</td></tr>
<tr><td>Assistant administrative officer, assistant audit officer, assistant prosecutorial officer, assistant broadcasting and telecommunications officer, assistant information systems officer, assistant facilities officer, assistant social welfare officer, assistant public health officer, assistant disaster safety officer, police inspector, or special-service official equivalent to Grade VII</td><td>39</td></tr>
<tr><td>Special-service official equivalent to Grade VIII</td><td>4</td></tr>
</table>

Notes

1. Of the authorized staff under this Table, the following positions shall be filled, respectively, by public officials belonging to the agencies specified:
- 1 person (1 senior official) from the Office for Government Policy Coordination or the Ministry of Strategy and Finance;
- 1 person (1 secretary) from the Office for Government Policy Coordination or the Ministry of Strategy and Finance;
- 4 persons (1 deputy audit officer, 2 audit senior officers and 1 assistant audit officer) from the Board of Audit and Inspection;
- 2 persons (1 broadcasting and telecommunications senior officer and 1 assistant broadcasting and telecommunications officer) from the Korea Communications Commission;
- 3 persons (1 administrative officer, 1 administrative senior officer and 1 assistant administrative officer) from the Office for Government Policy Coordination;
- 3 persons (1 administrative officer, 1 administrative senior officer and 1 assistant administrative officer) from the Ministry of Personnel Management;
- 4 persons (1 administrative officer, 1 administrative senior officer and 2 assistant administrative officers) from the Ministry of Strategy and Finance;
- 4 persons (2 administrative senior officers and 2 assistant administrative officers) from the Ministry of Education;
- 5 persons (1 prosecutorial investigation secretary, 1 prosecutorial officer or investigation officer, 2 prosecutorial senior officers and 1 assistant prosecutorial officer) from the Ministry of Justice;
- 7 persons (1 secretary or technical secretary, 2 administrative officers or information systems officers, 1 administrative senior officer, information systems senior officer or records researcher, and 3 assistant administrative officers, assistant information systems officers, assistant facilities officers or assistant disaster safety officers) from the Ministry of the Interior and Safety;
- 5 persons (1 administrative officer, social welfare officer or public health officer, 2 administrative senior officers, social welfare senior officers or public health senior officers, and 2 assistant administrative officers, assistant social welfare officers or assistant public health officers) from the Ministry of Health and Welfare;
- 4 persons (1 deputy director general or secretary, 2 administrative officers or maritime and fisheries officers, and 1 administrative senior officer or maritime and fisheries senior officer) from the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries;
- 3 persons (1 police senior inspector and 2 police inspectors) from the National Police Agency;
- 2 persons (1 police superintendent and 1 police senior inspector) from the Korea Coast Guard.

2. Where, after the completion of the Commission's investigative activities, its period of activity is extended under Article 7(2) of the Act to prepare and publish the comprehensive report and white paper under Article 47 of the Act, the authorized number of staff of the Commission shall, following analysis of the volume of work, job analysis and other relevant analysis, be set at the minimum number necessary for the Commission's activities.
